/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Cities continuously generate fragmented signals: trafficcameras, citizen complaints, weather feeds, emergency calls, water-level sensors, road sensorsand public-transport telemetry. The hard problem is not detecting each event independently; itisdeciding which observations belong to the same evolving incident and what is most likely causingit.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
63 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (For example, a sudden rise in water level, slowing traffic,repeated citizen reports and a blocked- road sensor may all be symptoms of one drainage failure.Aconventional dashboard shows four alerts. An operational system must infer one incident,preserve uncertainty, and update its understanding as new evidence arrives. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
